{
  "chapter_id": "08",
  "chapter_name": "餐廳用餐",
  "sentences": [
    {
      "id": "08-001",
      "en": "Do you have a table for two?",
      "keywords": [
        {
          "word": "table",
          "kk": "/ˈteɪbl/",
          "zh": "桌子"
        }
      ],
      "zh": "請問有兩人的桌位嗎？",
      "level": "A2",
      "tags": [
        "dining",
        "reservation",
        "arrival"
      ],
      "tips": "進入餐廳時的基本用語。若是大型聚餐，把人數改成對應數字即可，例如：a table for four（四人桌）。在熱門餐廳建議事先訂位（make a reservation）。",
      "audio": null,
      "type": "question"
    },
    {
      "id": "08-002",
      "en": "Could I see the menu, please?",
      "keywords": [
        {
          "word": "menu",
          "kk": "/ˈmɛnjuː/",
          "zh": "選單"
        }
      ],
      "zh": "可以給我看菜單嗎？",
      "level": "A2",
      "tags": [
        "dining",
        "menu",
        "ordering"
      ],
      "tips": "menu 是「菜單」。現在許多餐廳使用 QR code 點餐，你可以說：Do you have a QR code for the menu?（你們有掃描菜單的 QR code 嗎？）",
      "audio": null,
      "type": "question"
    },
    {
      "id": "08-003",
      "en": "I'd like to order the grilled salmon, please.",
      "keywords": [
        {
          "word": "grilled",
          "kk": "/ɡrɪld/",
          "zh": "烤"
        },
        {
          "word": "salmon",
          "kk": "/ˈsæmən/",
          "zh": "鮭魚"
        }
      ],
      "zh": "我想點烤鮭魚。",
      "level": "A2",
      "tags": [
        "dining",
        "ordering",
        "food"
      ],
      "tips": "salmon 的 l 不發音，讀作 /ˈsæmən/。點餐時用 I'd like to order... 或直接說 I'll have...。常見烹飪方式：grilled（烤）、fried（炸）、steamed（蒸）、baked（烘烤）。",
      "audio": null,
      "type": "statement"
    },
    {
      "id": "08-004",
      "en": "What do you recommend?",
      "keywords": [
        {
          "word": "recommend",
          "kk": "/ˌrɛkəˈmɛnd/",
          "zh": "推薦"
        }
      ],
      "zh": "您有什麼推薦嗎？",
      "level": "A2",
      "tags": [
        "dining",
        "ordering",
        "recommendation"
      ],
      "tips": "recommend 是「推薦」。問了之後，服務生通常會介紹今日特餐（today's special）或招牌菜（signature dish）。這也是一個了解當地特色料理的好機會。",
      "audio": null,
      "type": "question"
    },
    {
      "id": "08-005",
      "en": "I'm allergic to peanuts. Does this dish contain any?",
      "keywords": [
        {
          "word": "allergic",
          "kk": "/əˈlɜrdʒɪk/",
          "zh": "過敏的"
        },
        {
          "word": "peanuts",
          "kk": "/ˈpiːnʌts/",
          "zh": "花生"
        }
      ],
      "zh": "我對花生過敏。這道菜有花生嗎？",
      "level": "B1",
      "tags": [
        "dining",
        "allergy",
        "food safety"
      ],
      "tips": "allergic to 是「對…過敏」。食物過敏可能非常危險，一定要在點餐前清楚告知。常見食物過敏原：peanuts（花生）、shellfish（貝類）、gluten（麩質）、dairy（乳製品）。",
      "audio": null,
      "type": "question"
    },
    {
      "id": "08-006",
      "en": "Could I have my steak medium rare, please?",
      "keywords": [
        {
          "word": "medium rare",
          "kk": "/ˈmiːdiəm rɛr/",
          "zh": "三分熟"
        }
      ],
      "zh": "我的牛排可以做三分熟嗎？",
      "level": "B1",
      "tags": [
        "dining",
        "steak",
        "preference"
      ],
      "tips": "牛排熟度從生到全熟：rare（一分熟）、medium rare（三分熟）、medium（五分熟）、medium well（七分熟）、well done（全熟）。不確定自己喜歡什麼，可以先點 medium 嘗試。",
      "audio": null,
      "type": "question"
    },
    {
      "id": "08-007",
      "en": "Could we get some more water, please?",
      "keywords": [
        {
          "word": "more",
          "kk": "/mɔr/",
          "zh": "更多的"
        }
      ],
      "zh": "可以再給我們一些水嗎？",
      "level": "A2",
      "tags": [
        "dining",
        "drinks",
        "service"
      ],
      "tips": "在歐美許多餐廳，服務生不會主動續水，需要自行招手或詢問。Excuse me, could we get some more water? 是有禮貌的詢問方式。",
      "audio": null,
      "type": "question"
    },
    {
      "id": "08-008",
      "en": "Excuse me, I didn't order this.",
      "keywords": [
        {
          "word": "order",
          "kk": "/ˈɔrdɚ/",
          "zh": "命令"
        }
      ],
      "zh": "不好意思，我沒有點這道。",
      "level": "A2",
      "tags": [
        "dining",
        "complaint",
        "service"
      ],
      "tips": "上錯菜時，禮貌地告知服務生即可，不需要動怒。可以補充說：I ordered the pasta, not the pizza.（我點的是義大利麵，不是披薩。）",
      "audio": null,
      "type": "statement"
    },
    {
      "id": "08-009",
      "en": "Could we get the bill, please?",
      "keywords": [
        {
          "word": "bill",
          "kk": "/bɪl/",
          "zh": "帳單"
        }
      ],
      "zh": "可以給我們帳單嗎？",
      "level": "A2",
      "tags": [
        "dining",
        "payment",
        "bill"
      ],
      "tips": "bill 是英式英語的「帳單」；美式英語說 check（Could we get the check?）。兩種說法在各地都能被理解。在歐美大多不會自動送帳單，用餐完畢後需要主動要求。",
      "audio": null,
      "type": "question"
    },
    {
      "id": "08-010",
      "en": "Can we pay separately?",
      "keywords": [
        {
          "word": "separately",
          "kk": "/ˈsɛpərɪtli/",
          "zh": "分別地"
        }
      ],
      "zh": "我們可以分開結帳嗎？",
      "level": "A2",
      "tags": [
        "dining",
        "payment",
        "splitting"
      ],
      "tips": "separately 是「分別地」。也可以說：Can we split the bill?（我們可以分攤帳單嗎？）部分餐廳不提供分開結帳服務，可以事先詢問。",
      "audio": null,
      "type": "question"
    },
    {
      "id": "08-011",
      "en": "Is service charge included in the bill?",
      "keywords": [
        {
          "word": "service charge",
          "kk": "/ˈsɜrvɪs tʃɑrdʒ/",
          "zh": "服務費"
        }
      ],
      "zh": "帳單有含服務費嗎？",
      "level": "B1",
      "tags": [
        "dining",
        "payment",
        "tip"
      ],
      "tips": "service charge（服務費）是某些餐廳自動計入帳單的費用，約 10-20%。若已含服務費，小費（tip）可以不用另外給。在美國、加拿大等地，服務費通常不含在帳單內，小費是習慣必給的。",
      "audio": null,
      "type": "question"
    },
    {
      "id": "08-012",
      "en": "Do you have a non-smoking section?",
      "keywords": [
        {
          "word": "non-smoking",
          "kk": "/nɑn ˈsmoʊkɪŋ/",
          "zh": "禁煙"
        }
      ],
      "zh": "你們有禁菸區嗎？",
      "level": "A2",
      "tags": [
        "dining",
        "seating",
        "preference"
      ],
      "tips": "non-smoking section 是「禁菸區」；smoking section 是「吸菸區」。在許多國家，室內餐廳已全面禁菸（smoke-free），這個問題更適用於戶外用餐區或仍允許吸菸的地區。",
      "audio": null,
      "type": "question"
    },
    {
      "id": "08-013",
      "en": "Is this dish spicy?",
      "keywords": [
        {
          "word": "spicy",
          "kk": "/ˈspaɪsi/",
          "zh": "辛辣的"
        }
      ],
      "zh": "這道菜辣嗎？",
      "level": "A2",
      "tags": [
        "dining",
        "food",
        "preference"
      ],
      "tips": "spicy 是「辣的」。如果不吃辣，可以說：Could you make it less spicy?（可以做不那麼辣嗎？）或 I'd like it mild, please.（我要口味溫和的。）",
      "audio": null,
      "type": "question"
    },
    {
      "id": "08-014",
      "en": "Could I get this to go?",
      "keywords": [
        {
          "word": "to go",
          "kk": "/tə ɡoʊ/",
          "zh": "去"
        }
      ],
      "zh": "我可以把這個打包帶走嗎？",
      "level": "A2",
      "tags": [
        "dining",
        "takeout",
        "service"
      ],
      "tips": "to go 是美式說法，表示「外帶、打包帶走」；英式說法是 takeaway。吃不完想打包剩菜，可以說：Could I get a box for this?（可以給我一個打包盒嗎？）",
      "audio": null,
      "type": "question"
    },
    {
      "id": "08-015",
      "en": "The food was delicious. Thank you very much.",
      "keywords": [
        {
          "word": "delicious",
          "kk": "/dɪˈlɪʃəs/",
          "zh": "可口的"
        }
      ],
      "zh": "食物非常美味。非常感謝。",
      "level": "A2",
      "tags": [
        "dining",
        "compliment",
        "farewell"
      ],
      "tips": "delicious 是「非常美味的」。用餐結束後給予讚美是很好的餐廳禮儀，可以讓服務人員知道你很滿意。也可以說：Everything was wonderful!（一切都很棒！）",
      "audio": null,
      "type": "statement"
    }
  ],
